ersations about advice for a healthy lifestyle."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Identifies general information in short written and spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies general information in short written and spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies general information in short written and spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies general information in short written and spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies general information in short written and spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identifies general information in short written and spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Review of the Present Continuous and Be Going To"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Continuous</span> and <span class=\"strong\">be going to</span> to talk about future actions and events.<br>  <br>You use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Continuous</span> to talk about arrangements and plans. <span class=\"strong\">Be going to</span> puts an emphasis on the idea of intention (decide to do something).<br>   <br>You can use <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">intend to</span></span> in place of be going to.<br> "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'm starting school soon. vs. I'm going to start school next Monday.<br>  I intend to start school next week."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "stomach ache"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a pain in a person's stomach "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I have a stomach ache from the street food I ate."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le03ob11aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about travel."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "headache "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a pain in someone's head "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The hot sun is giving me a headache."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le03ob11aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "open-air"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "located outside "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We are going to an open-air market."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le03ob11aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "market"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a place where products are bought and sold"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The markets are filled with food!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le03ob11aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "active"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "describing a volcano that is likely to erupt"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Tomorrow we are going to visit an active volcano."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le03ob11aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "sick"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "affected by physical illness; unwell"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Eating junk food makes me feel sick."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le03ob11aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "windsurfing"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the sport of riding a board that is pushed by the wind "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm going to go windsurfing."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le03ob11aud07"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn4le03ob11re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Write a dialogue (8-10 sentences) about plans with your friend."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the model for help."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Practice your dialogue with a partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Switch parts and practice again."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example dialogue\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Jason</span>: Hey, Carol. What are you and Bill up to these days?<br/> <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Carol</span>: I'm going to go hiking tomorrow, and Bill is going to try windsurfing.<br/> <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Jason</span>: Wow! Sounds great.<br/> <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Carol</span>: What's new with you?<br/> <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Jason</span>: I'm planning to start school soon.<br/> <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Carol</span>: What are you going to study?<br/> <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Jason</span>: Italian!\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background\"}"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write a dialogue talking about my plans with a friend."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about plans and intentions in the near future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "My partner and I communicate about traveling."}]}], "type": "sena"}